{
  "_doc": "The town's own army (Systems/Army.cs). Regiments are townsfolk: a standing regiment takes recruits out of their trades into a training hall (buildings.json `trains`), drills them up from drillFloor of their strength to full over a unit's `drill` days and pays them a wage a day; the levy calls townsfolk up from their work under the town's laws (service: volunteers or conscription; pay: paid or unpaid). Strength is in the units of the defence at the walls (a watchman is 3). Each regiment stands at a post: walls (all of it in a siege), reserve (drills faster), patrol (the town guard: raids at night and the watch's eye) or guard (the mayor's guard: knives in the night). A hero in command adds leadership to as many soldiers as they can lead. Unit `needs`: institution:<id>, ally:<people id> (an allied settlement of that people), building:<id>.",
